WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.209 --> 00:00:05.270
"Criminal Minds" was one of the most successful
shows on television during its 15 seasons

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.270
on the air.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:10.660
The crime drama produced an astounding 324
episodes in that period of time, which is

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.950
a huge accomplishment for any series.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.609
For a while there, it even seemed like the
saga had finally closed the book, but fans

00:00:16.609 --> 00:00:20.899
of the CBS ratings smasher can rest assured
knowing that a highly anticipated revival

00:00:20.899 --> 00:00:24.069
will be available to stream on Paramount+
in the near future.

00:00:24.069 --> 00:00:28.180
That means the Behavioral Analysis Unit still
has yet more cases to crack in the future,

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.880
and it also means fans will get to spend more
time with all the show's characters, whether

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.390
they love them or loathe them.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:36.800
While the show's compelling murder mysteries
are a big part of the appeal, it was always

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.460
the characters themselves, and their relationships
with one another, that gave "Criminal Minds"

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.720
its heart, keeping viewers coming back, season
after season.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:47.429
Some of the protagonists are beloved fan favorites
whose company will never get old.

00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:51.410
Others, meanwhile, have made an impact for
the wrong reasons — even those played by

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:52.789
famous actors.

00:00:52.789 --> 00:00:56.340
Some of these well-regarded actors may have
some great credits to their name, but fans

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.000
of "Criminal Minds" can be pretty particular.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.440
Looking back, it appears that there was one
specific character who really angered the

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.030
fans, to the point where they even petitioned
to have the character written off the series.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:10.079
"Criminal Minds" was known for featuring the
occasional big name stars throughout the years,

00:01:10.079 --> 00:01:13.280
most of whom have been well-received by the
show's die-hard audience.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.110
That said, Jennifer Love Hewitt rubbed some
fans the wrong way, despite joining "Criminal

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:20.640
Minds" on the back of successful programs
like "The Ghost Whisperer" and movies such

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.670
as "I Know What You Did Last Summer."

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:26.930
Hewitt's character, Kate Callahan, first appeared
in the Season 10 premiere episode.

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:31.480
Presented as a stable, motherly figure with
a happy home life, albeit with a tragic past

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.229
— namely, a sister and brother-in-law who
were killed in the Pentagon attack on 9/11

00:01:35.229 --> 00:01:39.600
— she is also given relatable traits such
as an affinity for cute animal photos and

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.900
a love of karaoke.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.539
"Karaoke at the Benjamin."

00:01:42.539 --> 00:01:43.649
"Excuse me?"

00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:46.310
"You were singing karaoke at the Benjamin
the night it closed."

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:50.680
Considering that Hewitt herself is a popular
actress who often earns fan adoration in her

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:54.120
other work, the producers probably thought
that her character Kate was going to be an

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:55.470
instant hit with viewers.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:59.970
It didn't go that way — but to be fair,
the odds were firmly stacked against her success

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.119
from the get-go.

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:04.700
When the actress joined the series, she had
to fill the void left behind by Jeanne Tripplehorn,

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.829
who had played Alex Blake.

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:10.500
Critics of the newcomer believed that developing
a new character distracted from the more important

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.281
elements of the series.

00:02:12.281 --> 00:02:15.990
Now, Kate's warmth and familial ties certainly
earned her some die-hard fans.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:20.390
However, those who didn't agree with her inclusion
went to some drastic measures to try to have

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.390
her removed.

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.910
The dissatisfaction with Jennifer Love Hewitt's
character, believe it or not, even caused

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:29.330
one fan to launch a Change.org petition — titled,
rather straightforwardly, "Write Jennifer

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:33.170
Love Hewitt's character off Criminal Minds"
— claiming that she took away screen time

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.480
and distracted from the other agents and cases
in the BAU.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:39.790
Others explained that they just didn't like
the character and found Hewitt's performance

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.510
and the writing for her character to be hokey.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:46.060
For what it's worth, that particular petition
only acquired 42 signatures, but it highlighted

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.730
some of the issues some viewers had with the
new cast member.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:51.680
"There are dozens of us…

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:52.680
Dozens!"

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.330
In the end, Hewitt did depart from the popular
series ... but not for the reasons one might

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.590
expect, and not because of the petition.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.490
Hewitt did eventually give her critics their
wish, leaving "Criminal Minds" at the end

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.310
of the season in 2015.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:07.640
But it wasn't because of any fan gripes -- instead,
it was because she became pregnant with her

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:11.151
second child, and the due date — and her
desire to fully invest her time in the new

00:03:11.151 --> 00:03:14.950
arrival — conflicted with the time period
in which the show's eleventh season was set

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.080
to start shooting.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.730
Speaking to Entertainment Weekly, Criminal
Minds' showrunner Erica Messer explained,

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:23.760
"Jennifer wanted to be able to give this second
baby everything she gave her first, and that's

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:29.260
taking time off to be a full-time mom [...] We
wrote to that, and that's how season 10 ends."

